son:/inferences/0/argument\"]},\"definition_reviews\":{},\"source_reviews\":{\"M001\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Full-signature probe record gives theorem kind, exact signature, pins and axioms [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] (signature-evidence.json:4-20); official pinned source agrees: X has EMetricSpace, MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace, s:Set X, d:NNReal, hypothesis (d:ENNReal)<dimH s, conclusion μH[d] s=∞. The R application's intended X=ℝⁿ, s=E, d=s is compatible provided the Euclidean Borel structure and coercion are supplied; it does not establish the separate Hausdorff-content inference used after this result.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M001/0/sources/M001/signature\",\"signature-evidence.json:/M001/0/sources/M001/axioms\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:94-98\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:105-118\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/0\"]},\"M002\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The probe's full signature and axioms are present in signature-evidence.json:31-49, and the pinned official source confirms [Countable β], f:β→α→ENNReal, measure μ on measurable α, and the sole explicit hypothesis ∀i,AEMeasurable(f i) μ (Mathlib source lines 360-371). The prose application does not establish the claimed equality for its stated restricted Lebesgue measure/integrand; more importantly, it silently identifies the index-sum integral with the Hausdorff-cover cost without defining the restricted measure, the indicator-valued ENNReal functions, measurability of J_i∩I, or the integral calculation and normalizes the interval measure to length one without a stated proof. The declared hypothesis-check sentence is not that derivation. Thus source theorem is genuine but its actual cited use is not established.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M002/0/sources/M002/signature\",\"signature-evidence.json:/M002/0/sources/M002/axioms\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Add.lean:360-371\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/1/hypothesis_checks/0\"]}},\"structure_review\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"There is one proposition target P and one producer R001; all listed roots feed that inference and both M sources have actual application records. H roots match spec. Nevertheless AND-closure cannot accept P because the sole inference is mathematically unsupported. The unique inference also has no declared rules supporting its substantial Hausdorff measure/content and product-dimension arguments; citations do not close them. No packet replay was performed or claimed.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/propositions\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/inputs\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/output\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument\"]},\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/0/text\",\"premises\":\"H002 compactness, and the undeveloped assertion that for every q>D there are arbitrarily inexpensive positive-diameter covers with the stated scale controls.\",\"conclusion\":\"dim_H(E×I)≤D+1.\",\"reason\":\"The argument invokes Hausdorff-measure/dimension critical-exponent definitions and cover characterization, and handles replacement of zero-diameter members, without any declared result or complete derivation. ‘The definition gives H^q(E)=0’ and the asserted cover choice do not establish the exact scale-content claim from the stated inputs. Also q>D is not required nonnegative whereas the dimension measure exponent is NNReal.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"premises\":\"M001 gives H^s(E)=∞ and M002 gives integral of a countable ENNReal sum.\",\"conclusion\":\"Hausdorff content c_s(E,δ)≤c_(s+1)(F,δ), hence dim_H(F)≥s+1.\",\"reason\":\"No declared Hausdorff content definition/passage between infinite Hausdorff measure and scale content tending to infinity, or passage from content inequality to infinite Hausdorff measure/dimension, is supplied. The invented c_s is only a local definition of an infimum of Nat-indexed cover sums, with no stated relation to the mathlib Hausdorff measure. The integration/application calculation is incomplete as described in M002.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/2/text\",\"premises\":\"H001 and projection F→I.\",\"conclusion\":\"dim_H(F)≥1 when D=0, and equality for n=0.\",\"reason\":\"The dimension monotonicity of a Lipschitz surjection/projection and dim_H([0,1])=1 are imported mathematical results but neither is a declared source or proved in the argument. For n=0 the asserted isometry/dimension conclusion likewise has no derivation. The x₀ witness is unused.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals\",\"premises\":\"F is defined locally as E×[0,1], while target specifies concatenated Euclidean metric; R001 uses an arbitrary δ-cover and products/projections.\",\"conclusion\":\"all cover-diameter and projection statements apply to the target metric.\",\"reason\":\"The candidate does not state the metric on the locally defined F nor justify the displayed Euclidean metric correspondence or the asserted product diameter bound from the declared calculation policy. Zero-diameter cover elements and n=0 are not completely treated.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties